interface: 
=========
interface is blueprint it contain abstract methods and constants.
that can implement in the class.

Basic rules of Interfaces:
============================
    1.An interface defines a contract,it specifies what a class must be able to do.

     It will not provide the implementation,the implementation must be provided by the implemented class.

    syntax:
    -------
         interface InerfaceName{
            //variables
            double PI=3.14;internally it will vhange as publlic satic final double PI=3.14;
            //abstract
            //
         }


    2. Any class implimenting the interface must provide  implimention to interface's abstract methods.

    3.we cannot create object  for interface
    
    4.we cannot create consructor for interfaces
    
    5.we cannot create instance variables for instance
    
    6.when a variable is declared in interface it automatically because
      a public a static final.

        eg.     public final String method(){

              }
              
              
     7.Before java 8,interface allowed only abstract methods.
     
      java 8 has introduced   default and Static methods in interfaces.
      
      java 9+ has introduced private methods
     
     8. the class sin which we u se the interface must use keyword "impliments".
     
            eg. if MyInterface is an interface
            
           and MyClass is a class 
           
           then Myclass must use the interface  follows:
                  
                  Myclass impliments MyInterface;
                  
        9. Aclass can impliment  multiple interfaces ,
           this is reffered to as multiple interface implimentation.
           
        10.interface =contract/capability 
           abstract class =common base class with shared state and behaviour.
           
       11.we use interface when we only want to define a contract
          we use abstract classes when we wnat to common instace variables and state for an object
        
       12.we use abstract class when we need consructors ,interfaces cannot have consructors.
       
       13.when we  want to describe what an object "Is" then consider the abstract class.
       
	   14.when we want to describe what an object "Can Do" we consider the interfaces. 
